      "content": "```python\n\"\"\"\nLRU (Least Recently Used) Cache implementation with type hints and comprehensive unit tests.\n\nThis module provides a generic LRU cache that evicts the least recently used items\nwhen the cache reaches its maximum capacity.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Generic, TypeVar, Optional, Iterator, Tuple, List\n\n# Type variables for generic key and value types\nK = TypeVar('K')\nV = TypeVar('V')\n\n\nclass LRUCache(Generic[K, V]):\n    \"\"\"\n    A generic LRU (Least Recently Used) cache implementation.\n    \n    This cache stores key-value pairs and evicts the least recently used\n    item when the cache exceeds its maximum capacity. Accessing an item\n    (via get or put) marks it as recently used.\n    \n    Type Parameters:\n        K: The type of keys stored in the cache.\n        V: The type of values stored in the cache.\n    \n    Attributes:\n        capacity (int): The maximum number of items the cache can hold.\n        _cache (OrderedDict): Internal storage for key-value pairs, ordered by access time.\n    \n    Example:\n        >>> cache = LRUCache",
